==English==
[[Image:Valeriana officinalis jfg1.jpg|thumb|A '''valerian''' plant in bloom.]]
{{wikipedia|valerian (plant)}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fro|valeriane}} or {{der|en|ML.|valeriana}}, an early {{der|en|trk}} borrowing. See {{cog|ota|بالدران|tr=baldıran}} for further forms.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/vəˈlɪəɹɪən/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|Valyrian|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[hardy]] [[perennial]] [[flowering plant]], ''[[Valeriana officinalis]]'', with heads of [[sweet]]ly [[scent]]ed pink or white [[flower]]s.
# More generally, any plant of the genus ''[[Valeriana]]''.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The root of ''[[Valeriana officinalis]]'', used in herbal medicine.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Valeriana officinalis}} {{l|en|allheal}}, {{vern|cat thyme}}

